 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h2>Standard Types (Std_Types)</h2><p class=\"lead\">Standard types, return codes (Std_ReturnType, E_OK, E_NOT_OK), version info structures, and error codes shared across the entire AUTOSAR architecture.</p>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00005\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_ReturnType <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00005]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">typedef <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_00005\">Std_ReturnType</a>;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>This type can be used as standard API return type which is shared between the RTE and the BSW modules. It shall be defined as follows: typedef uint8 Std_ Return Type;</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00015\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_VersionInfoType <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00015]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">typedef struct {\n    <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00014\">uint16</a> vendorID;\n    <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00014\">uint16</a> moduleID;\n    <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> sw_major_version;\n    <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> sw_minor_version;\n    <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> sw_patch_version;\n} <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_00015\">Std_VersionInfoType</a>;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>This type shall be used to request the version of a BSW module using the <Module name>_ Get Version Info() function.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00021\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_TransformerError <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00021]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">typedef <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_00021\">Std_TransformerError</a>;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>-</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00024\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_TransformerClass <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00024]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">typedef <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_00024\">Std_TransformerClass</a>;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>-</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00027\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_TransformerForward <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00027]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">typedef <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_00027\">Std_TransformerForward</a>;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>- Tags: atp.Status=draft</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00029\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_TransformerForwardCode <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00029]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">typedef <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_00029\">Std_TransformerForwardCode</a>;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>- Tags: atp.Status=draft</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_91001\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_MessageType <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_91001]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>This type is used to encode the different type of messages. - Currently this encoding is limited to the distinction between requests and responses in C/ S c ommunication.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_91002\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_MessageResultType <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_91002]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">typedef <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a> <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_91002\">Std_MessageResultType</a>;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>This type is used to encode different types of results for response messages. - Currently this encoding is limited to the distinction between OK and ERROR responses.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_91003\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> Std_ExtractProtocolHeaderFieldsType <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_91003]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">typedef Std_ReturnType (*<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_91003\">Std_ExtractProtocolHeaderFieldsType</a>)(const <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00013\">uint8</a>* buffer, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"platform.html#SWS_Platform_00015\">uint32</a> bufferLength, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_91001\">Std_MessageTypeType</a>* messageType, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"#SWS_Std_91002\">Std_MessageResultType</a>* messageResult);</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Type for the function pointer to extract the relevant protocol header fields of the message and the type of the message result of a transformer. - At the time being, this is limited to the types used for C/ S communication (i.e., REQUE ST and RESPONSE and OK and ERROR).</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00006\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> E_OK / E_NOT_OK <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00006]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">#define E_OK 0x00u\n#define E_NOT_OK 0x01u</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Because E_ OK is already defined within OSEK, the symbol E_ OK has to be shared. To avoid name clashes and redefinition problems, the symbols have to be defined in the following way (approved within implementation): #ifndef STATUSTYPEDEFINED #define STATUSTYPEDEFINED #define E_ OK 0x00u typedef unsigned char Status Type; /* OSEK compliance */ #endif #define E_ NOT_ OK 0x01u</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00007\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> STD_HIGH / STD_LOW <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00007]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">#define STD_HIGH 0x01u\n#define STD_LOW 0x00u</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>The symbols STD_ HIGH and STD_ LOW shall be defined as follows: #define STD_ HIGH 0x01u /* Physical state 5V or 3.3V */ #define STD_ LOW 0x00u /* Physical state 0V */</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00013\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> STD_ACTIVE / STD_IDLE <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00013]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">#define STD_ACTIVE 0x01u\n#define STD_IDLE 0x00u</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>The symbols STD_ ACTIVE and STD_ IDLE shall be defined as follows: #define STD_ ACTIVE 0x01u /* Logical state active */ #define STD_ IDLE 0x00u /* Logical state idle */</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\" id=\"SWS_Std_00010\"><span class=\"kind\">type</span> STD_ON / STD_OFF <span class=\"sws\">[SWS_Std_00010]</span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">#define STD_ON 0x01u\n#define STD_OFF 0x00u</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>The symbols STD_ ON and STD_ OFF shall be defined as follows: #define STD_ ON 0x01u #define STD_ OFF 0x00u</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  }
 ]
}
